    "title": "Landslide (rainfall induced)",
    "description": "Landslide exposure is estimated using the GFDRR rainfall-triggered Global Landslide Hazard Map (V2), based on the annual frequency of significant rainfall-induced landslides per km². Children and population exposed are identified using 0.1 and 0.01 landslides/km² thresholds (Medium–High and Moderate hazard). Indicators include absolute and relative exposed population and normalized scores ranging from 0–10.",
